; Stage 15 W5c: `CStr` is FLOW-EXEMPT and a null-initialised `CStr` global must
; keep compiling.
;
; This fixture exists as a tripwire for a KNOWN, SEPARATE null-safety hole that
; W5c deliberately did not close: `defvar`'s global initializer is a constant
; renderer that never routes through `coerce-int-val`, so `pkind-flow-check`
; never runs and `(defvar g:ptr:Thing null)` compiles clean then segfaults at
; runtime, while the identical *local* binding is correctly rejected. Closing
; that is Stage 15 W6 (nullability).
;
; When W6 adds the missing pkind check to `defvar-init-ir`'s `null` branch, it
; must add it to the `TY-PTR` path ONLY. `CStr` is the C `char*` FFI type, where
; a null pointer is ordinary and meaningful, and is grouped with `void*` outside
; the Phase-F non-null regime by context/conventions.md's string-type lattice.
; If this file ever fails to compile, that carve-out has been lost.
(defvar g-null:CStr null)
(defvar g-noinit:CStr)

(defn main ():i32
  (if (= g-null null) (return 0) (return 1)))
